version: 2.0.2
title: catalogue: grice/incomplete-project
---
note[grice/incomplete-project]: Can't see the whole project

The rule `fixture/whole-project-view` sees every module of the project, but
grice couldn't read all of it, so it didn't run: `src/broken.gleam` doesn't
parse and `test/app_test.gleam` couldn't be read (No such file). A claim
about the whole project can't rest on part of it.

Hint: If `gleam build` accepts a module that doesn't parse, glance, which
grice reads Gleam code with, doesn't support its syntax yet, so please
report it to glance. Check that each file that couldn't be read is there
and that you can read it; a Gleam module must also be UTF-8.


